text":"12"}]}]},{"_key":"a6e","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6f","text":"16"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6g","text":"24"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6h","text":"50"}]}]},{"_key":"a6i","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6j","text":"17"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6k","text":"25"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6l","text":"6"}]}]},{"_key":"a6m","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6n","text":"18"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6o","text":"26"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6p","text":"13"}]}]},{"_key":"a6q","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6r","text":"19"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6s","text":"27"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6t","text":"6"}]}]},{"_key":"a6u","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6v","text":"19"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6w","text":"342 = 19×18"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a6x","text":"513 = 19×27"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}],"note":{"style":"band","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a4l","style":"normal","bare":true,"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a4m","text":"No. of suras = 19, Total of sura numbers = 342 = 19×18, Total of verses = 513 = 19×27"}]}]}}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a6z","n":7,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a72","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a71","text":"The word “Elaah” which means “god” occurs in Verses 9:129. The total occurrence of this word in the Quran is 95, 19×5. The inclusion of 9:128-129 causes this word to increase by 1, to 96."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a73","n":8,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a76","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a75","text":"The INDEX TO THE WORDS OF THE QURAN, lists 116 “Rasool” (Messenger) words. One of these words is in 9:128. By removing this false verse, 115 “Rasool” words remain. Another “Rasool” word which must be excluded from counting is in 12:50, since it refers to the “messenger of Pharaoh,” not the messenger of God. Thus, the total occurrence of “Rasool” of God is 114, 19×6."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a77","n":9,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a7a","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a79","text":"Another important word that occurs in the false Verses 9:128-129 is the word “Raheem” (Merciful). This word is used in the Quran exclusively as a name of God, and its total count is 114, 19×6, after removing the word “Raheem” of 9:128, which refers to the prophet. According to 7:188, 10:49, and 72:21 the Prophet did not possess any power of mercy."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a7b","n":10,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a7e","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7d","text":"The INDEX lists 22 occurrences of the word “‘Arsh” (Throne). After removing the false injection 9:129, and the “‘Arsh” of Joseph which occurs in 12:100, and the “‘Arsh” of the Queen of Sheba (27:23), we end up with 19 “‘Arsh” words. This proves that the word “‘Arsh” of 9:129 does not belong in the Quran."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a7f","n":11,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a7i","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7h","text":"The Quranic command “Qul” (Say) occurs in the Quran 332 times. Also, the word “Qaaloo” (They said) occurs the same number of times, 332. Since the false Verse 9:129 contains the word “Qul” (Say), its inclusion would have destroyed this typical Quranic phenomenon."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a7j","n":12,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a7m","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7l","text":"The Quran contains 6234 numbered verses and 112 un-numbered verses (Basmalahs). Thus, the total number of verses in the Quran is 6346, 19×334. The false Verses 9:128-129 violate this important criterion of the Quran’s code."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a7n","n":13,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a7q","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7p","text":"In addition to violating the numbers of words as listed above, 9:128-129 violate the Quran’s mathematical structure. When we add the number of verses in each sura, plus the sum of verse numbers (1+2+3+...+n, where n=number of verses), plus the number of each sura, the cumulative total for the whole Quran comes to 346199, or 19×19×959. This phenomenon confirms the authenticity of every verse in the Quran, while excluding 9:128-129. Table 3 is an abbreviated illustration of the calculations of Item 13. This phenomenon is impossible if the false Verses 9:128-129 are included."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a8v","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7r","text":"Table 3: Mathematical coding of the Quran’s suras & verses, based on “19”"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7s","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7t","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7u","text":"Sum of Verse #’s"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7v","text":"Total"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a7w","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7x","text":"1"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7y","text":"7"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a7z","text":"28"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a80","text":"36"}]}]},{"_key":"a81","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a82","text":"2"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a83","text":"286"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a84","text":"41041"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a85","text":"41329"}]}]},{"_key":"a86","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a87","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a88","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a89","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8a","text":"–"}]}]},{"_key":"a8b","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8c","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8d","text":"127"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8e","text":"8128"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8f","text":"8264"}]}]},{"_key":"a8g","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8h","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8i","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8j","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8k","text":"–"}]}]},{"_key":"a8l","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8m","text":"114"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8n","text":"6"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8o","text":"21"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8p","text":"141"}]}]},{"_key":"a8q","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8r","text":"6555"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8s","text":"6234"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8t","text":"333410"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8u","text":"346199 = 19×19×959"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a8w","n":14,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a8z","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a8y","text":"When we carry out the same calculations as in Item 13 above, but for the 85 un-initialed suras only, which include Sura 9, the cumulative total is also a multiple of 19. The cumulative total for all un-initialed suras is 156066, or 19×8214. This result depends on the fact that Sura 9 consists of 127 verses, not 129. The data are shown in Table 4. The false verses would have destroyed this criterion."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"aa2","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a90","text":"Table 4: Mathematical coding of the Quran’s 85 un-initialed suras"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a91","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a92","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a93","text":"Sum of Verse #’s"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a94","text":"Total"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a95","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a96","text":"1"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a97","text":"7"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a98","text":"28"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a99","text":"36"}]}]},{"_key":"a9a","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a9b","text":"4"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a9c","text":"176"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a9d","text":"15576"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a9e","text":"15756"}]}]},{"_key":"a9f","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a9g","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a9h","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a9i","text":"–"}]},{