e digit “9.” These are Sura 10 and Sura 104. By adding the sura number, plus the number of verses, plus the sum of verse numbers, from Sura 10 to Sura 104, we get a grand total that equals 23655, or 19×1245. The details are shown in Table 9. The inclusion of Sura 9 with the wrong number of verses, 129, would have altered both the sum of verse numbers and the cumulative total — the sum of verse numbers would have become 627+129=756, and the cumulative total would not be 23655 — and the Quran’s code would have been violated (Table 9)."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"aiq","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"agn","text":"Table 9: All the suras whose number of verses ends with “9”"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ago","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"agp","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"agq","text":"Sum of Verse #s"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"agr","text":"Total"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"ags","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"agt","text":"10"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"agu","text":"109"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"agv","text":"5995"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"agw","text":"6114"}]}]},{"_key":"agx","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"agy","text":"15"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"agz","text":"99"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ah0","text":"4950"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ah1","text":"5064"}]}]},{"_key":"ah2","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ah3","text":"29"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ah4","text":"69"}]},