type":"span","_key":"au5","text":"The numbers 127, 128 and 129 have two digits in common, “1” and “2.” Let us consider all the suras whose number of verses contains the digits 1 and 2. By adding the sura numbers plus the numbers of verses, we get 1159, 19×61. See Table 18. If Sura 9 consisted of 129 verses, the total would have become 1159+2 = 1161, not a multiple of 19."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"avf","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"au7","text":"Table 18: Suras whose final verse have the numerals “1” and “2” in common with the verses in question (127, 128, and 129)"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"au8","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"au9","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aua","text":"Total"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"aub","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"auc","text":"5"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aud","text":"120"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aue","text":"125"}]}]},{"_key":"auf","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aug","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"auh","text":"127"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aui","text":"136"}]}]},{"_key":"auj","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"auk","text":"11"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aul","text":"123"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aum","text":"134"}]}]},{"_key":"aun","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"auo","text":"16"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aup","text":"128"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"auq","text":"144"}]}]},{"_key":"aur","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aus","text":"21"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aut","text":"112"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"auu","text":"133"}]}]},{"_key":"auv","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"auw","text":"37"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aux","text":"182"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"auy","text":"219"}]}]},{"_key":"auz","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"av0","text":"65"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"av1","text":"12"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"av2","text":"77"}]}]},{"_key":"av3","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"av4","text":"66"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"av5","text":"12"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"av6","text":"78"}]}]},{"_key":"av7","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"av8","text":"92"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"av9","text":"21"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ava","text":"113"}]}]},{"_key":"avb","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avc","text":"322"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avd","text":"837"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ave","text":"1159 = 19×61"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"avg","n":34,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"avj","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avi","text":"Sura 9 is a single-digit sura whose number of verses contains the digits 1 and 2. There is only one other sura that possesses these traits: Sura 5 is a single-digit sura, and it consists of 120 verses. As shown in Table 19, the number of verses in these two suras is 120+127 = 247 = 19×13. If Sura 9 consisted of 129 verses, the total would have been 247+2 = 249, not a multiple of 19."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"avw","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avk","text":"Table 19: The only suras whose number is a single digit, and the number of verses contains the numerals “1” and “2”"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avl","text":"Sura Number"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avm","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"avn","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avo","text":"5"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avp","text":"120"}]}]},{"_key":"avq","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avr","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avs","text":"127"}]}]},{"_key":"avt","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avu","text":"Total ="}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avv","text":"247 = 19×13"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"avx","n":35,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"aw0","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"avz","text":"We looked at all the suras whose number of verses contains “1” and “2.” Let us now look at all the suras whose number of verses begins with the digit “1.” There are 30 suras that possess this quality: Suras 4, 5, 6, 9, 10, 11, 12, 16, 17, 18, 20, 21, 23, 37, 49, 60, 61, 62, 63, 64, 65, 66, 82, 86, 87, 91, 93, 96, 100, and 101. Their numbers of verses are 176, 120, 165, 127, 109, 123, 111, 128, 111, 110, 135, 112, 118, 182, 18, 13, 14, 11, 11, 18, 12, 12, 19, 17, 19, 15, 11, 19, 11, and 11. The sum of verse numbers (1+2+3+...+n) for these 30 suras is 126122, or 19×6638. If Sura 9 consisted of 129 verses, the sum of their verse numbers would have been 126122 + 128 + 129 = 126379, and this total is not a multiple of 19."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"aw1","n":36,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"aw4","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aw3","text":"Sura 9 consists of 127 verses, and 9+1+2+7 equals 19. Let us look at all the suras whose digits of sura and verses add up to 19. There are 10 suras that meet this specification, and the total of their sura numbers and numbers of verses is 1216, or 19×64. The data are shown in Table 20."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"axh","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aw5","text":"Table 20: All the suras where the digits of sura number and number of verses add up to 19"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aw6","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aw7","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aw8","text":"Total"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"aw9","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awa","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awb","text":"127"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awc","text":"136"}]}]},{"_key":"awd","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awe","text":"22"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awf","text":"78"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awg","text":"100"}]}]},{"_key":"awh","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awi","text":"26"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awj","text":"227"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awk","text":"253"}]}]},{"_key":"awl","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awm","text":"45"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awn","text":"37"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awo","text":"82"}]}]},{"_key":"awp","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awq","text":"54"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"awr","