},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a139","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13a","text":"Last 2 Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13b","text":"7’s in Last 2 Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a13c","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13d","text":"1"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13e","text":"6,7"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13f","text":"1"}]}]},{"_key":"a13g","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13h","text":"2"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13i","text":"285,286"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13j","text":"0"}]}]},{"_key":"a13k","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13l","text":"3"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13m","text":"199,200"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13n","text":"0"}]}]},{"_key":"a13o","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13p","text":"4"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13q","text":"175,176"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13r","text":"2"}]}]},{"_key":"a13s","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13t","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13u","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13v","text":"–"}]}]},{"_key":"a13w","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13x","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13y","text":"126,127"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13z","text":"1"}]}]},{"_key":"a140","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a141","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a142","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a143","text":"–"}]}]},{"_key":"a144","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a145","text":"25"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a146","text":"76,77"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a147","text":"3"}]}]},{"_key":"a148","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a149","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14a","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14b","text":"–"}]}]},{"_key":"a14c","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14d","text":"114"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14e","text":"5,6"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14f","text":"0"}]}]},{"_key":"a14g","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14h","text":"Total ="}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14i","text":"38 = 19×2"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a14l","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14k","text":"If the last verse in Sura 9 was 129 instead of 127, the number of occurrences of the digit “7” would have been 37, not 38, and this criterion would have been destroyed."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a14m","n":43,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a14p","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14o","text":"Assuming that Sura 9 consists of 129 verses, let us look at all the suras that contain a verse No. 129. This means that we look at all the suras that consist of 129 or more verses. For example, Sura 2 consists of 286 verses. Therefore, it contains a verse that is assigned the number “129.” We then take this verse and add it to all the other verses assigned the number 129 throughout the Quran. Under this assumption, there are 9 suras that contain a verse No. 129. Interestingly, we find that the total of sura numbers of these 9 suras is a multiple of 19 (114), while the total for the nine 129’s can be a multiple of 19 if 2 is deducted from their total. In other words, we are told that one of these 9 suras contains 2 extra verses. The details are in Table 27. When we add 114, plus 1161, and remove 2, we get 1273, or 19×67. Compare this total (1273) with the total reported in the Item 44 below. Of the 9 suras listed in Table 27, which one has the extra 2 verses? The answer is provided in Item 44."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a15p","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14q","text":"Table 27: All suras which contain a verse number “129”"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14t","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14u","text":"Verse No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a14v","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14w","text":"2"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14x","text":"129"}]}]},{"_key":"a14y","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14z","text":"3"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a150","text":"129"}]}]},{"_key":"a151","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a152","text":"4"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a153","text":"129"}]}]},{"_key":"a154","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a155","text":"6"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a156","text":"129"}]}]},{"_key":"a157","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a158","text":"7"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a159","text":"129"}]}]},{"_key":"a15a","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15b","text":"9 ?"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15c","text":"129"}]}]},{"_key":"a15d","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15e","text":"20"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15f","text":"129"}]}]},{"_key":"a15g","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15h","text":"26"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15i","text":"129"}]}]},{"_key":"a15j","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15k","text":"37"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15l","text":"129"}]}]},{"_key":"a15m","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15n","text":"114"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15o","text":"1161"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}],"note":{"style":"band","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a14r","style":"normal","bare":true,"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14s","text":"114 + 1161 − 2 = 1273 = 19×67"}]}]}}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a15q","n":44,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a15t","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15s","text":"To pinpoint the location of these two false verses, let us look at all the suras that contain a verse No. 128, while continuing to assume that Sura 9 consists of 129 verses. This will give us the same list of suras as in Table 27, and also bring in Sura 16 which has precisely 128 verses. As shown in Table 28, Sura 9 stands out in glaring disharmony; it is singled out as the sura that contains the false verses. The total of suras and verses becomes divisible by 19 only if Sura 9 is removed. Note that the divisible total, after removing Sura 9, is 1273, 19×67, which is the same total obtained in Item 43 above after removing 2 verses. This remarkable phenomenon proves that Sura 9 could not contain a verse No. 128."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a16w","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15u","text":"Table 28: All suras containing a verse number “128”"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15x","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15y","text":"Verse No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a15z","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a160","text":"2"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a161","text":"128"}]}]},{"_key":"a162","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a163","text":"3"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a164","text":"128"}]}]},{"_key":"a165","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a166","text":"4"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a167","text":"128"}]}]},{"_key":"a168","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a169","text":"6"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16a","text":"128"}]}]},{"_key":"a16b","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16c","text":"7"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16d","text":"128"}]}]},{"_key":"a16e","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16f","text":"9 ?"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16g","text":"128"}]}]},{"_key":"a16h","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16i","text":"16"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16j","text":"128"}]}]},{"_key":"a16k","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16l","text":"20"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16m","text":"128"}]}]},{"_key":"a16n","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16o","text":"26"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16p","text":"128"}]}]},{"_key":"a16q","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16r","text":"37"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16s","text":"128"}]}]},{"_key":"a16t","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16u","text":"130"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16v","text":"1280"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}],"note":{"style":"band","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a15v","style":"normal","bare":true,"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15w","text":"130 + 1280 = 1410 (not a multiple of 19). If we remove Sura 9, with its 128 verses, we get 1410 − 9 − 128 = 1273 = 19×67"}]}]}}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a16x","n":45,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a170","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16z","text":"Sura 9 is an un-initialed sura whose last two verses are 126 and 127. Let us take the 85 un-initialed suras, and add up the numbers of the last two verses in each sura. For example, the last two verses in Sura 1 are 6 and 7. Add 6+7 and you get 13. The next un-initialed sura is Sura 4; its last two verses are 175 and 176. Add 175+176 and you get 351. Do this for all un-initialed suras. The data are in Table 29. Thus, the last two verses of Sura 9 are confirmed to be 126 and 127."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a180","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a171","text":"Table 29: Abbreviated table of the last two verses in the un-initialed suras"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a172","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a173","text":"Last 2 Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a174","text":"Total"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a175","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a176","text":"1"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a177","text":"6+7"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a178","text":"13"}]}]},{"_key":"a179","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17a","text":"4"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17b","text":"175+176"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17c","text":"351"}]}]},{"_key":"a17d","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17e","text":"5"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17f","text":"119+120"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17g","text":"239"}]}]},{"_key":"a17h","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17i","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17j","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17k","text":"–"}]}]},{"_key":"a17l","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17m","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17n","text":"126+127"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17o","text":"253"}]}]},{"_key":"a17p","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17q","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17r","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17s","text":"–"}]}]},{"_key":"a17t","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17u","text":"114"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17v","text":"5+6"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17w","text":"13"}]}]},{"_key":"a17x","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17y","text":"Total ="}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17z","text":"6897 = 19×363"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a181","n":46,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a184","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a183","text":"Let us now take the last two verses in every sura in the Quran, initialed and un-initialed, and add the digits of the last two verses in each sura (Table 30). It is readily obvious that the last two verses of every sura in the Quran are divinely fixed, and divinely guarded through this intricate mathematical code. The last two verses of Sura 9 are confirmed to be 126 & 127, not 128 & 129."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a198","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a185","text":"Table 30: Sum of digits of the last two verses of every sura in the Quran"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a186","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a187","text":"Last 2 Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a188","text":"Sum of the Digits"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a189","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18a","text":"1"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18b","text":"6,7"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18c","text":"6 + 7"}]}]},{"_key":"a18d","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18e","text":"2"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18f","text":"285,286"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18g","text":"2+8+5+2+8+6"}]}]},{"_key":"a18h","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18i","text":"3"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18j","text":"199,200"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18k","text":"1+9+9+2+0+0"}]}]},{"_key":"a18l","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18m","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18n","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18o","text":"–"}]}]},{"_key":"a18p","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18q","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18r","text":"126,127"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18s","text":"1+2+6+1+2+7"}]}]},{"_key":"a18t","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18u","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18v","text":"–"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18w","text":"–"}]}]},{"_key":"a18x","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18y","text":"113"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18z","text":"4,5"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a190","text":"4 + 5"}]}]},{"_key":"a191","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a192","text":"114"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a193","text":"5,6"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a194","text":"5 + 6"}]}]},{"_key":"a195","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a196","text":"Total ="}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a197","text":"1824 = 19×96"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a199","n":47,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a19c","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19b","text":"Sura 9 consists of 127 verses, and 127 consists of 3 digits. Let us look at all the suras whose number of verses consists of 3 digits; these are suras 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 12, 16, 17, 18, 20, 21, 23, 26, and 37. Their verse numbers are 286, 200, 176, 120, 165, 206, 127, 109, 123, 111, 128, 111, 110, 135, 112, 118, 227, and 182, respectively. By taking the last digit in each number of verses, and adding up these digits, we get 6+0+6+0+5+6+7+9+3+1+8+1+0+5+2+8+7+2 = 76 = 19×4. If Sura 9 consisted of 129 verses, the last digit in its number of verses would be 9 instead of 7, and the total of last digits would be 78 instead of 76, and this phenomenon would disappear."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a19d","n":48,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a19g","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19f","text":"Let us look at the list of suras shown in Item 47 above. Since the number of verses in Sura 9 is an odd number, let us now consider the odd-numbered verse numbers. There are 8 suras with a 3-digit, odd number of verses: Suras 6, 9, 10, 11, 12, 17, 20, and 26. Their numbers of verses are 165, 127, 109, 123, 111, 111, 135, & 227. The last digits in these numbers of verses are 5, 7, 9, 3, 1, 1, 5, and 7, respectively, and the sum of these digits is 38, or 19×2. Obviously, if Sura 9 consisted of 129 verses, its last digit would be 9, not 7, and the sum of the last digits would be 40, not a multiple of 19. The detailed data are shown in Table 31. Thus, we are getting more and more specific, as we zoom in on the last digit in the number of verses."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a1ak","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19h","text":"Table 31: All suras whose number of verses is odd, and consists of 3 digits"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19i","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19j","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19k","text":"Last Digit"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a19l","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19m","text":"6"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19n","text":"165"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19o","text":"5"}]}]},{"_key":"a19p","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19q","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19r","text":"127"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19s","text":"7"}]}]},{"_key":"a19t","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19u","text":"10"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19v","text":"109"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19w","text":"9"}]}]},{"_key":"a19x","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19y","text":"11"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a19z","text":"123"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1a0","text":"3"}]}]},{"_key":"a1a1","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1a2","text":"12"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1a3","text":"111"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1a4","text":"1"}]}]},{"_key":"a1a5","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1a6","text":"17"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1a7","text":"111"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1a8","text":"1"}]}]},{"_key":"a1a9","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1aa","text":"20"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ab","text":"135"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ac","text":"5"}]}]},{"_key":"a1ad","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ae","text":"26"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1af","text":"227"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ag","text":"7"}]}]},{"_key":"a1ah","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ai","text":"Total ="}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1aj","text":"38 = 19×2"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1al","n":49,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1ao","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1an","text":"Let us continue to work with the same group of suras of Items 47 and 48. Since Sura 9 is an odd-numbered sura, let us now remove all the even-numbered suras from the list of suras shown in Item 47. Now we have odd-numbered suras, with odd-numbered verses. There are only three such suras in the whole Quran: 9, 11, and 17. Their numbers of verses are 127, 123, and 111 (Table 32). If Sura 9 consisted of 129 verses, this remarkable phenomenon would have been destroyed."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a1b4","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ap","text":"Table 32: Odd numbered suras whose number of verses is odd and consists of 3 digits"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1aq","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ar","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a1as","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1at","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1au","text":"127"}]}]},{"_key":"a1av","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1aw","text":"11"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ax","text":"123"}]}]},{"_key":"a1ay","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1az","text":"17"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1b0","text":"111"}]}]},{"_key":"a1b1","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1b2","text":"Total ="}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1b3","text":"361 = 19×19"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1b5","n":50,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1b8","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1b7","text":"Let us continue to work with the three suras listed in Item 49. These are all the suras in the Quran whose number is odd (like Sura 9), their number of verses consists of 3 digits (like Sura 9), and their number of verses is also odd (like Sura 9). As shown in Table 32, the verse numbers of these 3 suras are 127, 123, and 111. Just add the individual digits, and you get 1 + 2 + 7 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 19. Obviously, this phenomenon depends on the now proven truth that Sura 9 consists of 127 verses. If Sura 9 consisted of 129 verses, the only suras in the Quran that possess the above stated qualities would have added up to 1+2+9+1+2+3+1+1+1 = 21. In other words, this important component of the Quran’s mathematical code would have disappeared."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1b9","n":51,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1bc","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bb","text":"There are three suras (1) whose numbers are odd, (2) their numbers of verses are odd, and (3) the number of verses consists of 3 digits. They are Suras: 9, 11, and 17 (see Items 48 through 50 for the flow of this point). Just add the individual digits that make up the three sura numbers, and you get 9+1+1+1+7=19."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1bd","n":52,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1bg","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bf","text":"The number 129 is divisible by 3. If Sura 9 consisted of 129 verses as the distorters claimed, then it would be (1) an odd-numbered sura that (2) consists of a 3-digit number of verses, (3) the number of verses is odd, and (4) the number of verses is divisible by 3. There are only two suras in the whole Quran that possess these qualities: Sura 11 with 123 verses, and Sura 17 with 111 verses. The sum of digits of both sura numbers and the numbers of verses comes to 1+1+1+2+3+1+7+1+1+1 = 19. This can be observed only if Sura 9 consists of 127 verses."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1bh","n":53,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1bk","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bj","text":"Sura 9 is (1) odd-numbered, (2) its number of verses is odd, (3) its number of verses ends with the digit “7,” (4) its number of verses is a prime number, and (5) the sura number is divisible by 3 & 9. The only two suras that possess these qualities are: Sura 9 (127 verses), and Sura 45 (37 verses). Just add the digits you see:"}]},{"_type":"appendixStatement","_key":"a1bl","text":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bm","text":"9+1+2+7=19 & 4+5+3+7=19; Total for both suras = 19+19 = 38."}]}}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1bn","n":54,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1bq","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bp","text":"Let us assume that Sura 9 does have 129 verses. In that case we will have only two suras in the whole Quran whose number begins with 9, and their number of verses ends with 9: Sura 9 (129 verses) and Sura 96 (19 verses). As detailed in Table 33, the grand total of sura number, plus the number of verses, plus the sum of verse numbers is 8828, not a multiple of 19."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a1cd","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1br","text":"Table 33: Suras whose numbers begins with “9” and their number of verses ends with “9”"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bu","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bv","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bw","text":"Sum of Verse #s"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bx","text":"Total"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a1by","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bz","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1c0","text":"129?"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1c1","text":"8385"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1c2","text":"8523"}]}]},{"_key":"a1c3","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1c4","text":"96"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1c5","text":"19"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1c6","text":"190"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1c7","text":"305"}]}]},{"_key":"a1c8","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1c9","text":"105"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ca","text":"148"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1cb","text":"8575"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1cc","text":"8828"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}],"note":{"style":"band","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1bs","style":"normal","bare":true,"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1bt","text":"(Not a multiple of 19)"}]}]}},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1cf","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ce","text":"Now let us remove the false verses (128 & 129) from Sura 9, and repeat the same calculations. The result of this correction is shown in Table 34. The grand total becomes 8569, 19×451."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a1d0","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1cg","text":"Table 34: Same data as in Table 33, after correcting the number of verses in Sura 9"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ch","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ci","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1cj","text":"Sum of Verse #s"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ck","text":"Total"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a1cl","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1cm","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1cn","text":"127"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1co","text":"8128"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1cp","text":"8264"}]}]},{"_key":"a1cq","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1cr","text":"96"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1cs","text":"19"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ct","text":"190"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1cu","text":"305"}]}]},{"_key":"a1cv","style"