":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1mh","n":61,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1mk","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1mj","text":"The phrase “LAA ELAAHA ELLA HOO” occurs 7 times between the missing Basmalah of Sura 9 and the extra Basmalah of Sura 27, in 9:31, 11:14, 13:30, 20:8, 20:98, 23:116, and 27:26. By adding the numbers of the 7 verses, we get 323, or 19×17. The detailed data are shown in Table 40."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a1nc","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ml","text":"Table 40: Occurrences of the phrase “LAA ELAAHA ELLA HOO” from the missing Basmalah to the extra Basmalah"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1mm","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1mn","text":"Verse Numbers With Phrase"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a1mo","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1mp","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1mq","text":"31"}]}]},{"_key":"a1mr","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ms","text":"11"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1mt","text":"14"}]}]},{"_key":"a1mu","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1mv","text":"13"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1mw","text":"30"}]}]},{"_key":"a1mx","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1my","text":"20"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1mz","text":"8"}]}]},{"_key":"a1n0","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1n1","text":"20"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1n2","text":"98"}]}]},{"_key":"a1n3","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1n4","text":"23"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1n5","text":"116"}]}]},{"_key":"a1n6","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1n7","text":"27"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1n8","text":"26"}]}]},{"_key":"a1n9","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1na","text":"Total ="}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1nb","text":"323 = 19×17"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]},{"_type":"appendixCallout","_key":"a1nd","tone":"muted","style":"remark","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1ne","style":"normal","bare":true,"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1nf","text":"If 9:129 were part of the Quran, the total in Table 40 would have been: 323 + 129 = 452, not a multiple of 19. God rejects what the hypocrites utter, even if it is the truth (63:1)."}]}],"reveal":false}]},{"_type":"appendixDivider","_key":"a1ng","title":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1nh","text":"The Ultimate Quranic Miracle"}]},"centered":true},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1ni","n":62,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1nn","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1nk","text":"Brother Abdullah Arik has discovered what I consider to be the ultimate Quranic miracle. This miraculous phenomenon incontrovertibly authenticates every single verse in the Quran — the number of verses in every sura, and the numbers assigned to every single verse in the Quran — while exposing and rejecting the false injections, 9:128-129. To witness this great phenomenon, see Page "},{"_type":"appendixLink","_key":"a1nl","n":1},{"_type":"span","_key":"a1nm","text":" (under the heading: Superhuman Numerical Combinations). Putting the number of every verse in the Quran in sequence from the beginning to the end, with the number of verses in each sura ahead of the verse numbers of each sura, the final number consists of 12692 digits (19×668), and the number itself is also a multiple of 19. If the wrong number of verses for Sura 9 was used — 129 instead of 127 — neither the number of digits, nor the number itself would be divisible by 19."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1no","n":63,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1nr","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1nq","text":"Since the subject of this Appendix is Sura 9 and its number of true verses, it is noteworthy that if we write down the number of the sura, 9, followed by the correct number of verses, 127, followed by the numbers of all the verses from 1 to 127, the resulting long number is a multiple of 19. Needless to say, if the wrong number of verses is used, i.e., 129 instead of 127, this remarkable miracle would have disappeared:"}]},{"_type":"appendixCallout","_key":"a1ns","tone":"muted","style":"result","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1nu","style":"mono","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1nt","text":"9 127 1 2 3 4 5 ..... 122 123 124 125 126 127."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1nw","style":"caption","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1nv","text":"The total number of verses in Sura 9 is followed by the numbers of every verse in the sura from 1 to 127. The resulting long number is a multiple of 19."}]}],"reveal":false}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1nx","n":64,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1o0","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1nz","text":"The number of verses in Sura 9, 127, is an odd number. The falsifiers added two fake verses, and this made the number of verses 129, which is also an odd number. Mr. Arik used the same computer program he devised for Item 62 above to check all odd-numbered verses in the Quran. Thus, the number of verses in every sura was written down, followed only by the last digit of each of the odd-numbered verses in that sura. Sura 1 was represented by the number 71357. Sura 2 was represented by the number 28613579.....5, and so on through the last sura. The result is a long number, with 3371 digits, that is divisible by 19. Obviously, Sura 9 was represented by the number 12713579......7:"}]},{"_type":"appendixCallout","_key":"a1o1","tone":"muted","style":"result","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1o3","style":"mono","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1o2","text":"7 1 3 5 7 286 1 3 5 ... 3 5 ...... 5 1 3 5 6 1 3 5."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1o5","style":"caption","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1o4","text":"The number of verses in every sura is followed by the numbers of the odd-numbered verses. The resulting long number, 3371 digits, is a multiple of 19."}]}],"reveal":false}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1o6","n":65,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1o9","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1o8","text":"Since Sura 9 is an un-initialed sura, Mr. Arik applied the same computer program to all 85 un-initialed suras. The number of every verse in each of the 85 suras was written down, without the number of verses in the sura. Thus, Sura 1 was represented by the number 1234567, not 71234567. This was done with all un-initialed suras. The final result is a number that consists of 6635 digits, and is a multiple of 19. These awesome phenomena would be destroyed if we used the wrong number of verses for Sura 9, i.e., 129 instead of 127."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixDivider","_key":"a1oa","title":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ob","text":"God’s Messenger of the Covenant Destined to Purify the Quran"}]},"centered":true},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1oc","n":66,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1oh","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1oe","text":"Finally, in a profound demonstration of the foreknowledge of the Almighty Author of the Quran, it is mathematically coded that “The person destined to prove that Sura 9 consists of 127 verses is Rashad Khalifa, God’s Messenger of the Covenant” (see "},{"_type":"appendixLink","_key":"a1of","n":2},{"_type":"span","_key":"a1og","text":"). The item presented here is another one of those numerous proofs; it is chosen for its relevance to this Appendix. The gematrical value of the word “Rashad,” as written in the Quran (40:29, 38) is 505 (R=200, Sh=300, A=1, and D=4). The gematrical value of the word “Khalifa,” as written in the Quran (38:26) is 725 (Kh=600, L=30, I=10, F=80, and H=5). By writing down the value of “Rashad,” followed by the value of “Khalifa,” followed by the number of Sura 9, followed by the correct number of verses in this sura, the product is 5057259127. This number is a multiple of 19; it equals 19×266171533."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1oi","n":67,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1ol","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ok","text":"The number of verses from 3:81, where God’s Messenger of the Covenant is prophesied, to 9:127, the end of Sura 9, is 988 (19×52). Table 41."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1om","n":68,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1op","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1oo","text":"The sum of verse numbers from 3:81 to 9:127 is also a multiple of 19 (Table 41)."}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a1ps","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1oq","text":"Table 41: The number of verses from 3:81 to the end of Sura 9"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1or","text":"Sura No."}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1os","text":"No. of Verses"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ot","text":"Sum of Verse #s"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a1ou","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ov","text":"3"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ow","text":"119"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ox","text":"16860"}]}]},{"_key":"a1oy","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1oz","text":"4"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1p0","text":"176"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1p1","text":"15576"}]}]},{"_key":"a1p2","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1p3","text":"5"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1p4","text":"120"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1p5","text":"7260"}]}]},{"_key":"a1p6","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1p7","text":"6"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1p8","text":"165"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1p9","text":"13695"}]}]},{"_key":"a1pa","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pb","text":"7"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pc","text":"206"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pd","text":"21321"}]}]},{"_key":"a1pe","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pf","text":"8"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pg","text":"75"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ph","text":"2850"}]}]},{"_key":"a1pi","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pj","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pk","text":"127"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pl","text":"8128"}]}]},{"_key":"a1pm","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pn","text":"988"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1po","text":"85690"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]},{"_key":"a1pp","style":"totalsPlain","cells":[{"children":[]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pq","text":"(19×52)"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pr","text":"(19×4510)"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a1qk","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pt","text":"Table 42: Occurrence of the word “God” from 3:78 to the end of Sura 9"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pu","text":"Sura Number"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapPrimary"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1pv","text":"Frequency of “God”"}]},"headerStyle":"leftNowrap","cellStyle":"tightMonoNowrapFaded"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a1pw","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1px","text":"3"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1py","text":"132"}]}]},{"_key":"a1pz","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1q0","text":"4"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1q1","text":"229"}]}]},{"_key":"a1q2","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1q3","text":"5"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1q4","text":"147"}]}]},{"_key":"a1q5","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1q6","text":"6"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1q7","text":"87"}]}]},{"_key":"a1q8","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1q9","text":"7"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qa","text":"61"}]}]},{"_key":"a1qb","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qc","text":"8"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qd","text":"88"}]}]},{"_key":"a1qe","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qf","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qg","text":"168"}]}]},{"_key":"a1qh","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qi","text":"Total ="}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qj","text":"912 = 19×48"}]}],"cellStyles":["monoPrimaryNowrap","monoPrimaryNowrap"]}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1ql","n":69,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1qo","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qn","text":"In Verse 3:78, just 3 verses before proclaiming God’s Messenger of the Covenant, the word “God” number 361 (19×19) occurs. This verse (3:78) informs us that some falsifiers will “add falsehood to the Quran, then claim that it is part of the Quran; they attribute lies to God, knowingly.”"}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1qp","n":70,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1qs","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qr","text":"The word “God” occurs 912 times (19×48) from Verse 3:78, which exposes the falsifiers, to 9:127."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1qt","n":71,"marker":"primary","body":"evidenceBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1qw","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qv","text":"The number of letters, plus the number of words in 3:78 and in the false verses 9:128-129, give the same total, 143. Verse 3:78 consists of 27 words and 116 letters, & 9:128-129 consist of 115 letters and 28 words."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixFigure","_key":"a1qx","src":"/appendices/app24_arabic.png","alt":"Arabic","width":371,"height":128,"frame":"sm"},{"_type":"appendixDivider","_key":"a1qy","title":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1qz","text":"What Can We Say?"}]},"centered":true},{"_type":"appendixSection","_key":"a1rb","style":"prose","tag":"section","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1r1","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1r0","text":"The overwhelming physical evidence provided by the Almighty to protect and authenticate His message leaves no doubt that: (1) no distortion of any kind can enter the Quran, (2) Verses 9:128-129 do not belong in the Quran, and (3) every element in the Quran is mathematically structured far beyond human capabilities — the number of suras, the number of verses, the numbers assigned to the suras and verses, the frequency of occurrence of key expressions, the number of words, the number of letters, and the unique and often uncommon spelling of certain words."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1r3","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1r2","text":"This Appendix documents a profound miracle in its own right. Vast and utterly overwhelming as it is, it does not surpass or even match the overall mathematical miracle of the Quran which is detailed in Appendix One. This merely confirms the fact that the Almighty Author of the Quran has deliberately permitted the blasphemous addition of two verses to Sura 9 in order to:"}]},{"_type":"appendixCallout","_key":"a1r4","tone":"primary","style":"summary","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1r6","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1r5","text":"(1) Demonstrate an essential function of the Quran’s mathematical composition."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1r8","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1r7","text":"(2) Prove the impossibility of tampering with the Quran."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1ra","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1r9","text":"(3) Fulfill God’s promise to distinguish the believers and expose the hypocrites."}]}]}]},{"_type":"appendixDivider","_key":"a1rc","title":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1rd","text":"Why Did God Permit It For 1400 Years ??"}]},"centered":true},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1rf","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1re","text":"Due to the mass corruption of Islam shortly after the prophet Muhammad’s death, God obviously has fulfilled His pledge in 47:38. A divine decree issued in Sura 47, which is entitled “Muhammad,” Verse 38 (19×2), stipulates that “if the Arabs failed to uphold the Quran, God will dismiss them from His grace, and substitute other people in their place.”"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1rh","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1rg","text":"When the Arabs distorted the Quran a few years after the Prophet’s death, and exterminated the Prophet’s family in the process, they incurred God’s pledge of 47:38, and no longer deserved to possess the Quran; the true Quran. The evidence is irrefutable that the Arabs have abandoned the Quran en masse."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1rj","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ri","text":"For example, there is not a single mosque in the so-called Muslim world today (1989) that upholds the crucial commandment: “The mosques belong to God; you shall not invoke anyone else besides God” (72:18)."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1rl","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1rk","text":"The call to prayer (Azan) and the prayer itself are no longer devoted to God alone; Muhammad’s name is invariably invoked along with the name of God."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1rp","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1rm","text":"The “First Pillar of Islam” is clearly stated in the Quran, 3:18 & 47:19, and its words are decreed to be: LAA ELAAHA ELLA ALLAH (There is no other god besides God). But the Muslims, as early as the first century AH, do not want God if Muhammad is not invoked along with Him. This is easily demonstrable today by going into any mosque and declaring: “LAA ELAAHA ELLA ALLAH;” this will actually enrage today’s Muslims. This behavior is documented in the Quran, 39:45. Moreover, my own research has now convinced me that the traditional Muslims are forbidden by God from uttering the Quranic, divinely dictated Shahaadah: “Ash-hadu Allaa Elaaha Ellaa Allah.” They can never say this Shahaadah (without invoking Muhammad’s name). Test them yourself. The First Pillar of the distorted Islam, LAA ELAAHA ELLA ALLAH, MUHAMMAD RASOOL ALLAH, does not conform with God’s commandments that came to us through Muhammad (see "},{"_type":"appendixLink","_key":"a1rn","n":13},{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ro","text":")."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1rr","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1rq","text":"A number of other commandments are violated as well by this Mohammedan Shahaadah. For example, the Quran enjoins us repeatedly from making any distinction among God’s messengers (2:136, 285; 3:84). The distorted Shahaadah gives more distinction to Muhammad, against his will. Despite the Quran’s repeated assertions that it is “complete, perfect, and fully detailed” (6:19, 38, & 114), the “Muslims” have refused to believe their Creator; they uphold such ridiculous and nonsensical sources as Hadith and Sunna. This unanimous rebellion against God and His messenger, and the mass reversion to glaring idolatry — idolizing the Prophet and the saints — called for fulfillment of God’s pledge in 47:38."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1rz","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1rs","text":"In view of the incontrovertible divine evidence presented here, and in Appendices "},{"_type":"appendixLink","_key":"a1rt","n":1},{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ru","text":", "},{"_type":"appendixLink","_key":"a1rv","n":2},{"_type":"span","_key":"a1rw","text":", and "},{"_type":"appendixLink","_key":"a1rx","n":26},{"_type":"span","_key":"a1ry","text":", one can truly appreciate the following verses:"}]},{"_type":"appendixVerseCards","_key":"a1sc","style":"stackedWide","body":"sm","refStyle":"spaced","entries":[{"_key":"a1s0","body":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1s1","text":"Surely, we have revealed this message, and surely, we will preserve it."}]},"wrapper":"plain","reference":{"children":[{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a1s2","reference":"15:9"}]}},{"_key":"a1s3","body":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1s4","text":"Say, “If all the humans, and all the jinns, banded together, in order to produce a Quran like this, they will surely fail, no matter how much assistance they lend one another.”"}]},"wrapper":"divided","reference":{"children":[{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a1s5","reference":"17:88"}]}},{"_key":"a1s6","body":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1s7","text":"The disbelievers rejected this message when it came to them, though it is a profound scripture. No falsehood can enter it, through addition or deletion. For it is a revelation from the Most Wise, Most Praiseworthy."}]},"wrapper":"divided","reference":{"children":[{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a1s8","reference":"41:41-42"}]}},{"_key":"a1s9","body":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1sa","text":"If we revealed this Quran to a mountain, you would see it trembling, crumbling, out of reverence for God."}]},"wrapper":"divided","reference":{"children":[{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a1sb","reference":"59:21"}]}}]},{"_type":"appendixCallout","_key":"a1sd","tone":"neutral","style":"aside","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1se","style":"normal","bare":true,"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1sf","text":"I acknowledge with thanks the valuable contributions of Mahmoud Ali Abib, Gatut Adisoma, Abdullah Arik, Ihsan Ramadan, Lisa Spray, and Edip Yuksel. Some of the astounding mathematical facts presented in this Appendix were discovered by these hard working researchers at Masjid Tucson."}]}]}]$pt$::jsonb, NULL, NULL),

-- Appendix 25: End of the World
('25', $pt$[{"_type":"appendixVerseCards","_key":"a4","style":"centerTight","body":"base","refStyle":"plain","entries":[{"_key":"a1","body":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2","text":"“(God is) the Knower of the future; He does not permit anyone to unveil such knowledge. Only through the messengers that He chooses does He reveal future and past events.”"}]},"wrapper":"none","reference":{"children":[{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a3","reference":"72:27"}]}}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ac","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a5","text":"Among the duties charged to me as God's Messenger of the Covenant is unveiling the end of the world. We learn from "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a6","reference":"18:7"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a7","text":"-8 and "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a8","reference":"69:13"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a9","text":"-15 that this world will come to an end. A new earth and new heavens will replace the present heavens and earth ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"aa","reference":"14:48"},{"_type":"span","_key":"ab","text":")."}]},{"_type":"appendixDivider","_key":"ad","title":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ae","text":"Signs of the Approaching End of the World"}]}},{"_type":"appendixSection","_key":"a1w","style":"proseTight","tag":"section","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"ai","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"af","text":"The Quran provides many signs, and states that the means for unveiling the end of the world have been given ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"ag","reference":"47:18"},{"_type":"span","_key":"ah","text":"). The signs given in the Quran include:"}]},{"_type":"appendixSection","_key":"a1v","style":"stackSm","tag":"div","content":[{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"aj","n":1,"marker":"primary","body":"rowBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"am","style":"term","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"al","text":"The splitting of the moon"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ao","style":"body","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"an","text":"This already happened in June 1969 when we landed on the moon and brought back moon rocks. People on earth can go now to many museums, colleges and observatories to look at pieces of the moon."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"ap","n":2,"marker":"primary","body":"rowBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"au","style":"term","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ar","text":"Discovering the Quran's 19-based mathematical code ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"as","reference":"74:30-37"},{"_type":"span","_key":"at","text":")"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"aw","style":"body","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"av","text":"Fulfilled in 1969-1974."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"ax","n":3,"marker":"primary","body":"rowBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a12","style":"term","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"az","text":"The creature ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a10","reference":"27:82"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a11","text":")"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a14","style":"body","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13","text":"\"Made from the earth, it alerts the people that they have been oblivious to their Creator.\" The Creature, made from the earth, did appear and was instrumental in unveiling the Quran's numerical code, and proclaiming that the world has neglected God's message; the creature is the computer. Note that the digits that make up 27:82 add up to 19."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a15","n":4,"marker":"primary","body":"rowBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1a","style":"term","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17","text":"Appearance of God's Messenger of the Covenant ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a18","reference":"3:81"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a19","text":")"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1c","style":"body","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1b","text":"As detailed in Appendix 2, a consolidating messenger, prophesied in the Quran, comes after all the prophets have delivered the scriptures, to purify and unify. This prophecy was fulfilled in Ramadan 1408."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1d","n":5,"marker":"primary","body":"rowBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1i","style":"term","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1f","text":"The Smoke ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a1g","reference":"44:10"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a1h","text":")"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1k","style":"body","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1j","text":"Occurs after God's Messenger of the Covenant has delivered the unified message and proclaimed Submission (Islam) as the only religion acceptable by God."}]}]},{"_type":"appendixEvidence","_key":"a1l","n":6,"marker":"primary","body":"rowBody","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a1s","style":"term","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1n","text":"Gog and Magog ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a1o","reference":"18:94"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a1p","text":", "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a1q","reference":"21:96"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a1r","text":")"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a1u","style":"body","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1t","text":"They re-appear, in accordance with God's plan, in the year 1700 AH (2271 AD). Gog and Magog are mentioned in 18:94 and 21:96. If you count the verses from 18:94 to the end of Sura 18, you find them 17. If you count the verses from 21:96 to the end of Sura 21, you find them also 17. This is the Quran's sign that Gog and Magog will re-appear in 1700 AH."}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"appendixDivider","_key":"a1x","title":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1y","text":"It Will Not Remain Hidden"}]}},{"_type":"appendixSection","_key":"a2l","style":"prose","tag":"section","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a22","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a1z","text":"Verse 15 of Sura 20 informs us that the end of the world will be revealed by God before the end of the world ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a20","reference":"20:15"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a21","text":"), and Sura 15, Verse 87, gives the time for that event:"}]},{"_type":"appendixCallout","_key":"a23","tone":"primary","style":"centeredTight","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a25","style":"semibold","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a24","text":"“We have given you the seven pairs, and the great Quran.”"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a27","style":"noteMono","children":[{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a26","reference":"15:87"}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a2d","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a28","text":"The seven pairs are the 14 Quranic Initials. The total gematrical value of these profound pillars of the Quran's miracle pinpoints the year of the end of the world. It is noteworthy that Verse 85 of Sura 15 states: “The end of the world will surely come to pass.” The next verse, "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a29","reference":"15:86"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a2a","text":", tells us that God is the Creator of this world, and, of course, He knows when it will end. The following verse, "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a2b","reference":"15:87"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a2c","text":", tells us when the world will end."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a2k","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2e","text":"As shown in Table 1, the gematrical values of “The Seven Pairs” of Quranic Initials total 1709 (see also Table 1 of "},{"_type":"span","_key":"a2g","text":"Appendix 1","marks":["a2f"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a2h","text":"). According to "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a2i","reference":"15:87"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a2j","text":", the world will survive for 1709 lunar years from the time this prophecy is stated in the Quran. This means that the world will end in the year 1710 AH — a multiple of 19: 1710 = 19×90."}],"markDefs":[{"_key":"a2f","_type":"link","href":"/appendices/1"}]}]},{"_type":"appendixDataTable","_key":"a4d","caption":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2m","text":"Table 1: Total Gematrical Value of “The Seven Pairs” of Quranic Initials"}]},"table":"collapse","columns":[{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2n","text":"#"}]},"headerStyle":"left","cellStyle":"tightMonoMuted"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2o","text":"Quranic Initial"}]},"headerStyle":"left","cellStyle":"tightMonoPrimaryMedium"},{"header":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2p","text":"Gematrical Value"}]},"headerStyle":"right","cellStyle":"tightMonoRight"}],"rows":[{"_key":"a2q","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2r","text":"1"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2s","text":"Q"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2t","text":"100"}]}]},{"_key":"a2u","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2v","text":"2"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2w","text":"N"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2x","text":"50"}]}]},{"_key":"a2y","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2z","text":"3"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a30","text":"S (Saad)"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a31","text":"90"}]}]},{"_key":"a32","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a33","text":"4"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a34","text":"H.M."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a35","text":"48"}]}]},{"_key":"a36","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a37","text":"5"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a38","text":"Y.S."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a39","text":"70"}]}]},{"_key":"a3a","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3b","text":"6"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3c","text":"T.H."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3d","text":"14"}]}]},{"_key":"a3e","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3f","text":"7"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3g","text":"T.S."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3h","text":"69"}]}]},{"_key":"a3i","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3j","text":"8"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3k","text":"A.L.M."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3l","text":"71"}]}]},{"_key":"a3m","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3n","text":"9"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3o","text":"A.L.R."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3p","text":"231"}]}]},{"_key":"a3q","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3r","text":"10"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3s","text":"T.S.M."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3t","text":"109"}]}]},{"_key":"a3u","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3v","text":"11"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3w","text":"`A.S.Q."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3x","text":"230"}]}]},{"_key":"a3y","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a3z","text":"12"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a40","text":"A.L.M.S."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a41","text":"161"}]}]},{"_key":"a42","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a43","text":"13"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a44","text":"A.L.M.R."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a45","text":"271"}]}]},{"_key":"a46","style":"data","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a47","text":"14"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a48","text":"K.H.Y.`A.S."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a49","text":"195"}]}]},{"_key":"a4a","style":"totalsPrimary","cells":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a4b","text":"Total ="}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a4c","text":"1709"}]}],"cellStyles":["mutedRight","monoPrimaryRight"]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a4l","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a4e","text":"The unveiling of this information took place in the year 1400 AH, 309 years before the prophesied end of the world (1709 - 1400 = 309). The number 309 is a Quranic number ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a4f","reference":"18:25"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a4g","text":"), and is connected with the end of the world ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a4h","reference":"18:21"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a4i","text":"). The peculiar way of writing 309 in "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a4j","reference":"18:25"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a4k","text":" — “Three hundred years, increased by nine” — indicates that the 309 are lunar years. The difference between 300 solar years and 300 lunar years is 9 years."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a4n","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a4m","text":"The year of this discovery, 1400 AH, coincided with 1980 AD, and 1980 plus 300 solar years is 2280, which is also a multiple of 19: 19×120. Thus the world ends in 1710 AH (19×90), which coincides with 2280 AD (19×120)."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a5f","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a4o","text":"For the disbelievers who do not accept these powerful Quranic proofs, the end of the world will come suddenly ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a4p","reference":"6:31"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a4q","text":", "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a4r","reference":"6:44"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a4s","text":", "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a4t","reference":"6:47"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a4u","text":"; "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a4v","reference":"7:95"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a4w","text":", "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a4x","reference":"7:187"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a4y","text":"; "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a4z","reference":"12:107"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a50","text":"; "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a51","reference":"21:40"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a52","text":", "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a53","reference":"22:55"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a54","text":"; "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a55","reference":"26:202"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a56","text":"; "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a57","reference":"29:53"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a58","text":"; "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a59","reference":"39:55"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5a","text":"; "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a5b","reference":"43:66"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5c","text":"; and "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a5d","reference":"47:18"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5e","text":")."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a5o","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a5g","text":"While Hadith is forbidden as a source of religious teachings ("},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5i","text":"Appendix 19","marks":["a5h"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5j","text":"), it can be a useful source of history. We can derive a lot of information about historical events and local customs and traditions during the early centuries of Islam. The books of Hadith indicate that the Quranic Initials were believed to determine the life span of the Muslim "},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5k","text":"Ummah","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5l","text":". The classic exegesis by Al-Baydaawy cites the following historical event as a possible explanation of the Quranic Initials. The same event is detailed in Al-Suyooty's "},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5m","text":"Itqaan","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5n","text":" (First Printing, 1318 AH, Vol 2, Page 10):"}],"markDefs":[{"_key":"a5h","_type":"link","href":"/appendices/19"}]},{"_type":"appendixCallout","_key":"a5p","tone":"neutral","style":"outlineQuote","content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"a5r","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a5q","text":"The Jews of Medina went to the Prophet and said, “Your Quran is initialed with A.L.M., and these Initials determine the life span of your religion. Since ‘A’ is 1, ‘L’ is 30, and ‘M’ is 40, this means that your religion will survive only 71 years.” Muhammad said, “We also have A.L.M.S.” They said, “The ‘A’ is 1, the ‘L’ is 30, the ‘M’ is 40, and the ‘S’ is 90. This adds up to 161. Do you have anything else?” The Prophet said, “Yes, A.L.M.R.” They said, “This is longer and heavier; the ‘A’ is 1, ‘L’ is 30, ‘M’ is 40, and ‘R’ is 200, making the total 271.” They finally gave up, saying, “We do not know how many of these Initials he was given!”"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a5t","style":"noteSource","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a5s","text":"[Al-Suyuty's Famous Reference: Itqaan]"}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a5v","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a5u","text":"Although this narration is well known, many scholars have been reluctant to accept the unmistakable connection between the Quranic Initials and the end of the world. They could not bring themselves to deal with this subject for the simple reason that the calculation makes the end of the world, and judgment, a reality."}]}]$pt$::jsonb, 'D1SfcV27g3k', 'Appendix 25 — End of the World'),

-- Appendix 26: The Three Messengers of Islam
('26', $pt$[{"_type":"appendixVerseCards","_key":"a4","style":"centerTight","body":"base","refStyle":"plain","entries":[{"_key":"a1","body":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a2","text":"“God took a covenant from the prophets, saying, ‘After I have given you the scripture and wisdom, a messenger will come to confirm what you have. You shall believe in him and support him.’”"}]},"wrapper":"none","reference":{"children":[{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a3","reference":"3:81"}]}}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"af","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a5","text":"This appendix provides the Quranic mathematical evidence that (1) Abraham was the original messenger of Islam, i.e., Submission ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a6","reference":"22:78"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a7","text":"), (2) Muhammad was the scripture-delivering messenger ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"a8","reference":"47:2"},{"_type":"span","_key":"a9","text":"), and (3) Rashad is the purifying and consolidating messenger who delivered the religion's authenticating proof ("},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"aa","reference":"3:81"},{"_type":"span","_key":"ab","text":" & "},{"_type":"span","_key":"ad","text":"Appendix 2","marks":["ac"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ae","text":")."}],"markDefs":[{"_key":"ac","_type":"link","href":"/appendices/2"}]},{"_type":"appendixDivider","_key":"ag","title":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ah","text":"Perpetual and Verifiable Evidence"}]}},{"_type":"block","_key":"am","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ai","text":"[1] As pointed out in "},{"_type":"span","_key":"ak","text":"Appendix 2","marks":["aj"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"al","text":", the gematrical value of “Abraham” is 258, the gematrical value of “Muhammad” is 92, the gematrical value of “Rashad” is 505, and 258+92+505 = 855 = 19×45."}],"markDefs":[{"_key":"aj","_type":"link","href":"/appendices/2"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ao","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"an","text":"[2] If we include “Ismail,” whose gematrical value is 211, and “Isaac,” whose gematrical value is 169, we still end up with a total gematrical value of 855+211+169 = 1235 = 19×65. The total gematrical value of the three messengers, or the five, cannot conform with the Quran's 19-based mathematical code if either Abraham, Muhammad, or Rashad is not included."}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"au","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ap","text":"[3] The first and last occurrences of “Abraham” are in "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"aq","reference":"2:124"},{"_type":"span","_key":"ar","text":" and "},{"_type":"quranRef","_key":"as","reference":"87:19"},{"_type":"span","_key":"at","text":". By adding the sura numbers, plus the number of verses, plus the sum of verse numbers from the first occurrence to the last occurrence, the grand total is 333,260 = 19×17540 (Table 1)."}]},{"_type":"appendixDivider","_key":"av","title":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"aw","text":"Table 1: Suras & Verses — First to Last Occurrence of Abraham"}]}},{"_type":"appendixGridTable","_key":"a2d","headers":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ax","text":"Sura No."}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ay","text":"No. of Verses"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"az","text":"Sum of Verse #s"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a10","text":"Total"}]}],"rows":[{"variant":"data","cells":[{"content":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a11","text":"2"}]}},{"content":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a12","text":"163"}]}},{"content":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a13","text":"33415"}]}},{"content":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a14","text":"33580"}]}}]},{"variant":"data","cells":[{"content":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a15","text":"3"}]}},{"content":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a16","text":"200"}]}},{"content":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a17","text":"20100"}]}},{"content":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a18","text":"20303"}]}}]},{"