of 127 verses, not 129 (see "},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5i","text":"Appendix 24","marks":["a5h"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5j","text":"). The sum of digits of 127 is 1+2+7=10. By finding all the verses whose digits add up to 10, from the missing "},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5k","text":"Basmalah","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5l","text":" of Sura 9 to the extra "},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5m","text":"Basmalah","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5n","text":" of Sura 27, then adding the number of these verses to the total number of verses from the missing "},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5o","text":"Basmalah","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5p","text":" to the extra "},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5q","text":"Basmalah","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5r","text":", we get 2128 = 19×112 (Table 3)."}],"markDefs":[{"_key":"a5h","_type":"link","href":"/appendices/24"}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"a5y","style":"normal","children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a5t","text":"[10] Sura 9 is an odd-numbered sura whose number of verses (127) is also odd. From the missing "},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5u","text":"Basmalah","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5v","text":" to the extra "},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5w","text":"Basmalah","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"a5x","text":", there are 7 suras that possess this property; they are odd-numbered suras whose numbers of verses are also odd. As detailed in Table 4, these are Suras 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 25, and 27. By adding the digits that make up the sura numbers and the numbers of verses, the grand total is 114 = 19×6."}]},{"_type":"appendixDivider","_key":"a5z","title":{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a60","text":"Table 3: The Verse Whose Digits Add Up to 10, from the Missing Basmalah to the Extra Basmalah"}]}},{"_type":"appendixGridTable","_key":"a7t","headers":[{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a61","text":"Sura No"}]},{"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"a62","text":"No. of Verses"}]},{"children"